                "{{domain}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Registers a new user account in the Express-YouTube API.\n\n- **Method & URL**: `POST {{domain}}/users/register`\n    \n- **Auth**: No authentication required; this is a public sign-up endpoint.\n    \n- **Body type**: `multipart/form-data`\n    \n\n### Request body fields\n\n- `fullName` (string, required): User’s full display name. Example: `Kirtan Gajjar`.\n    \n- `email` (string, required): User’s email address. Must be unique and in valid email format. Example: `kitten@gmail.com`.\n    \n- `password` (string, required): User’s password. The server may enforce minimum length/complexity rules.\n    \n- `username` (string, required): Public username/handle for the account. Must be unique. Example: `kitten`.\n    \n\n### Typical responses\n\n- **201 Created / 200 OK**: User registered successfully. The response usually includes basic user details and/or an auth token depending on server implementation.\n    \n- **400 Bad Request**: Missing or invalid fields (e.g., invalid email format, weak password, missing required fields).\n    \n- **409 Conflict**: Email or username already in use.\n    \n- **500 Internal Server Error**: Unexpected server-side failure while creating the account.\n    \n\nUse this endpoint to create a new user that can later authenticate and interact with the API."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\r\n    \"email\": \"kitten@gmail.com\",\r\n    \"password\": \"1234\"\r\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{domain}}/users/login",
              "host": [
                "{{domain}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "This endpoint logs in a user using their email and password.\n\n## Request\n- **Method:** `POST`\n- **URL:** `{{domain}}/users/login`\n- **Body (JSON):**\n  - `email` (string, required): The user’s email address.\n  - `password` (string, required): The user’s password.\n\n## Successful Response (Typical)\nOn success, the server returns a 2xx status code (commonly `200 OK`) with a JSON body that typically includes:\n- User information (e.g., id, name, email, etc.).\n- An authentication token (e.g., JWT or session token) that the client can use for subsequent authenticated requests.\n\n## Failure Response (Typical)\nOn failure, the server returns a 4xx status code (such as `400 Bad Request` or `401 Unauthorized`) with a JSON body that typically includes:\n- An error message indicating why the login failed (for example, invalid email/password combination or missing fields).\n\nThe `{{domain}}` variable in the URL should be set in the active environment to point to the correct API base URL (e.g., development, staging, or production)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
